        "check → scripts/check-skill.py; lints → scripts/check-lints.sh proves every lint in lints/lints.toml fires",
        "examples → check-examples.py compiles every Rust example; tests → unittest discover over unit · contracts · integration · e2e",
        "tests/contracts pins the pairing: lints.toml + clippy.toml + lints/check harness stay one three-file unit",
        "The contracts below are **unbreakable and non-waivable**: developers cannot opt out, and neither can you. When a gate fires, the fix is to re-cut the layout — never to weaken or delete the lints, and never to silence it with `#[allow]` or a lazy workaround.",
        "review flags any deleted lints entry or #[allow] on the diff itself, loudly — a broken contract is an automatic Must fix"
      ]
